ROOT CONDITION
  getStoreDetails() runs `if (slug.isNotEmpty) setStoreAddressToUserAddress(store lat/lng)`,
  i.e. a deep link relocates the user address onto the store's own coordinates. When those
  coordinates fall outside every zone polygon, /api/v1/config/get-zone-id returns 404
  ("location: inZone=false") and /api/v1/module then yields an EMPTY list. moduleTypeFor()
  matches store.moduleId against that empty list and returns null, so isFood/isGrocery are
  both false and every module-gated block is skipped.
  In-zone deep links are unaffected (store 1 and store 39 render correctly by deep link).

  Not a one-off fixture quirk — stores whose coordinates lie outside all zone polygons:
    grocery 273 | food 3 | pharmacy 1   (status=1)
  It is also a normal real-world path: any shared link to a store outside the recipient's zone.

WIRE IS NOT AT FAULT
  /api/v1/stores/details/sushi-world and /api/v1/stores/details/6 are byte-identical
  (same key set, no differing values). schedules len=7 days=[0..6] under all 7 header
  combinations tried (zoneId+moduleId / zoneId / moduleId / none / empty moduleId /
  wrong moduleId / wrong zoneId).

AVAILABLE FALLBACKS THE FIX DOES NOT USE
  store.moduleId is present and correct (=2 for store 6, =1 for stores 2/3), and the deep-link
  route itself carries `module=<id>`. The app has enough information to resolve the module
  without ModuleController.moduleList.

NOTE: the previously-reported "third shape" (schedules non-empty but no row matching today ->
